text.paragraph:
SABRIL is indicated as monotherapy for pediatric patients with infantile spasms 1 month to 2 years of age for whom the potential benefits outweigh the potential risk of vision loss [see 
                           Warnings and Precautions (5.1)
                           ].

If a decision is made to discontinue SABRIL, the dose should be gradually reduced [see Dosage and Administration (2.2, 2.3) and  
                           Warnings and Precautions (5.6)
                           ].

